{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Arm out for me. I'll grab the obs before Dr Shah starts.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes, of course. On the platform I counted my pulse, it was about 120.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (DOCTOR): Dr Shah. What happened.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): I had a sudden tightness in my chest on the train, and I thought I was having a heart attack.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (DOCTOR): When.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Three days ago. Err, Tuesday morning, on the way to the office.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (DOCTOR): Pain with it?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Not painful. It was tightness, across the chest.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (DOCTOR): Short of breath?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (DOCTOR): Shaking, or fear?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes. I was shaking and, umm, I felt very frightened. I am still a little shaky now.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (DOCTOR): Before this, ever?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Never. This was the first time.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): Palpitations right now?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really. Not at the moment.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): Cough?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (DOCTOR): Sweating?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Not that either.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (DOCTOR): Recreational drugs?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): No. I have never taken drugs.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (DOCTOR): Smoke? Drink?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): I have never smoked. I have a glass of wine with dinner, perhaps twice a week.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): The carriage was dreadfully crowded. Someone had a dog in a pram, which was irrelevant, I suppose.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any long-term conditions.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): I have asthma. I have had it since I was a child.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (DOCTOR): Wheeze from it lately?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): No... well, sometimes. Umm, if I run for the train.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (NURSE): Sorry. Your partner's just phoned the front desk. I'm putting her on speaker.",
  "[SEG0031] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Mia here, I'm on shift. He sleeps badly, tossing most nights. And he doesn't take his tablets on Sundays, I keep seeing them in the pack.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): The sleep is quite right, though I cannot date the start, last winter or the winter before, I truly cannot say. On the tablets I must correct you, it is Saturdays, not Sundays.",
  "[SEG0033] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Right, Saturdays. Oh, and the cut on his knuckle from the fence, that healed in five days.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes. It healed in the usual fashion.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (DOCTOR): Which tablets. Dose.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Montekulast. Ten milligrams by mouth at night, for the asthma. I miss Saturday.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (DOCTOR): Allergies to anything.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): No. None.",
  "[SEG0039] person_3 (DOCTOR): Stressed at work before it happened?",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm, I suppose. Sometimes, not really.",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (NURSE): Obs just now. Pulse is 84. He'd said 120 from the platform, not the figure I've got. Blood pressure 128 over 76, sats 99 percent, temp 36.7, resps 16.",
  "[SEG0042] person_3 (DOCTOR): Lungs clear, no wheeze, heart sounds normal, pulse regular. Provisionally this is a panic attack. I can't rule out a rhythm disturbance until the ECG.",
  "[SEG0043] person_3 (DOCTOR): We'll do an ECG today, and I'll show you slow breathing, in for four and out for six, to use if the tightness starts again. Back in two weeks, reception will book it. If you collapse or it lasts more than twenty minutes, go to emergency.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): I understand. Thank you, doctor. I shall practise the breathing."
 ],
